{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Whoever lies with his aunt.</b> This verse comes to teach about the karet stated above, that its punishment is childlessness." "<b>Childless.</b> As the Targum renders: without children. Similar to it: ״וְאָנֹכִי הוֹלֵךְ עֲרִירִי״ (Genesis 15). He has children — he buries them; he has no children — he dies without children. Therefore Scripture changed in these two verses: עֲרִירִים ״יָמֻתוּ״, עֲרִירִים ״יִהְיוּ״. <b>Childless they shall die.</b> If he has them at the time of the transgression, he will not have them when he dies, because he buries them in his lifetime. <b>Childless they shall be.</b> If he has none at the time of the transgression, he will be all his days as he is now (Sifra; Yevamot 55)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:29.377680193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}